  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligated $514M in FY2026 to date. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics recorded 217,597 awards with an average award size of $2.4K. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligations fell 31.8% year over year. Year-to-year totals show a peak in FY25 at $753M, followed by lower totals in FY26. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics top markets in FY2026 to date are concentrated in warehousing, petroleum product manufacturing, and adhesives, led by Other Warehousing and Storage at $172M and Petroleum Lubricating Oil and Grease Manufacturing at $118M. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics also has notable obligations in Adhesive Manufacturing at $61.2M and several manufacturing and wholesale categories between $59.4M and $3.8M. The fiscal-year totals are partial. The dataset lists contract obligations and some total contract values for largest awards and expiring contracts, and the FY2026 figures reflect fiscal year to date activity rather than a full-year total.",
